// Back in the 2000s: The Game — Draft #2 missions M08 "Extended Weekend" and M09 "Schnucks Sux".
// BOOK: "Week 4 - October 6th 2003" (PDF pp. 44–53) and "Week 4 - October 8th 2003" (PDF pp. 54–58).
// All book text lives in D8 / D9 (book order, spelling as printed). '' = Chris's narration. Nothing in D8 / D9 is game-original.
// Fixed by the book, whatever the player does: Milo drives. Zeke buys the tickets. Zeke jumps in the river (cutscene only).
// The power goes out, the flights move to the morning, and it was never Columbus Day. Dad grounds Chris: school, home, work.
// In M09 Chris tackles an innocent man, the real thief leaves during the confusion, and nothing about it is scored as a win.
// Adaptation notes (flagged for the author, not silent fixes):
//  - Chesterfield, Lambert and San Antonio are small story sets reached by a card; the Belleville map is not connected to them.
//  - The ticket counter and security are a scripted comedy beat exactly as written. There is nothing to sneak past or solve.
//  - The November 1987 passage is narrated in the first person ("me and Eric"), so those lines are spoken by "Jacob (2003)".
//  - The book lists Sam as "CaptianSammi06" / "CaptianSammi08" on these pages; the game keeps CaptainSammi06 until the author decides.
//  - The radio beat plays as narration only. No song is played.
